<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#nobility">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nobility</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nobility is a social class found in many societies that have an aristocracy, normally appointed by and ranked immediately below royalty. The term derives from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> nobilitas; in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> the nobiles were the families, patrician or plebeian, descended from someone who had held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">consulship</a>. In feudal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> the nobility were generally those who held a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fief">fief</a>, often land or office, in exchange for allegiance and mainly military services to a suzerain, and it became a hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> with fiscal and other privileges, as in pre-revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. By the 21st century noble status had become a largely honorary dignity in most societies.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Nobility</b> now survives mainly as a social distinction, though by one recent estimate aristocratic and gentry families still own nearly a third of England’s land, and traditional nobilities keep their standing in many African and Asian societies.</blockquote><a href="/government/aristocracy">Aristocracy · Impact &amp; Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Nobility</b> passed through the male line.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ancien-regime-france">Social Hierarchy of Ancien Régime France</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Nobility</b> was hereditary or personal: Peter the Great’s Table of Ranks granted personal nobility in its lower grades and hereditary nobility higher up, until 1845 at the eighth civil grade.</blockquote><a href="/societies/russian-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Russian Empire</a></li></ul></section>
